 answer="A Chandigarh to Dharamshala taxi covers about <b>240 km in 5.5–6.5 hours</b> via Kharar, Ropar, Kiratpur Sahib, Anandpur Sahib, Una, Amb, Dehra and Kangra; McLeodganj is 10 km further up. One-way fares start around <b>" + _S(240, 1.1) + " for a sedan</b>, <b>" + _O("ertiga", 240, 1.1) + " for an Ertiga</b> and <b>" + _O("crysta", 240, 1.1) + " for an Innova Crysta</b>; tolls, parking and the Himachal entry fee are extra. Leave by 7 am.",
 facts=[("Distance","~240 km"),("Drive time","5.5–6.5 hrs"),("Route","Ropar → NH503 via Una"),("Altitude","~350 m → ~1,450 m"),("McLeodganj","+10 km · ~2,080 m"),("Sedan from",_S(240, 1.1) + " one-way")],
 stops=[("Chandigarh · Mohali · Panchkula","Pickup at IXC airport arrivals, Chandigarh railway station, ISBT-43 or ISBT-17, or any address in the Tricity and Zirakpur."),
        ("Kharar · Kurali","Out of the Tricity on the Kharar flyover and north to Kurali — usually 45 minutes if you beat the morning office traffic."),
        ("Ropar","The road crosses the Sutlej at Ropar (Rupnagar); a good place for tea and a fuel top-up."),
        ("Kiratpur Sahib · Anandpur Sahib","At Kiratpur the Manali traffic turns right; you stay on NH503 past the white domes of Takht Sri Kesgarh Sahib at Anandpur Sahib — a short darshan stop is easy."),
        ("Nangal · Una","Past the Nangal barrage the car enters Himachal near Mehatpur, where the entry fee is paid, and crosses Una — the usual lunch stop."),
        ("Amb · Mubarikpur · Dehra","Low Shivalik hills along NH503. Chintpurni temple is a short detour from Mubarikpur and Jawalamukhi a short one from Dehra — add either when you book."),
        ("Ranital · Kangra","The Kangra valley opens up with the Dhauladhar wall ahead. Kangra fort and the Brajeshwari Devi temple are right in town."),
        ("Dharamshala · McLeodganj","Drop in lower Dharamshala, or 10 km up to McLeodganj, Bhagsu, Dharamkot or Naddi, as close to your hotel as the one-way lanes allow.")],
